# run33 (2026-09-23 22:42-22:53 -03): the withdrawn colour-format series ported onto Mohamed Ahmed's
#   nouveau-imp-upstr-v120 (Linux 7.3-rc1) as local branch ycbcr-poc, tip f970f8e60:
#   CD=5 fix + NVC57D OCSC/clamp + head conversion + Broadcast RGB + YCbCr 4:4:4/4:2:2 + 4:2:0 (GA102+,
#   untestable here) + DVI properties. Mode --ycbcr: run27+run28 matrix, 22 steps x 30 s, no module swap.
# Sink: KDL-46EX725 (model 11266, 2011) over the 10 m cable, RTX 3060 (GA106), HDMI-A-2.
# Result, Daniel's table verbatim ("OSD" = bit depth confirmed on the OSD; 8-bit shows nothing):
#   "all pass, no issues. Not a single time I had to enable 3D by hand."
#   RGB 12 - F [pass osd] L [pass osd] A [pass osd]; 10 - F [pass osd] L [pass osd]; 8 - F [pass osd] L [pass osd]
#   YUV 4:4:4 - 12 [pass osd] 10 [pass osd] 8 [pass osd]; 4:2:2 - 12 [pass] 10 [pass] 8 [pass osd]
#   SBS 4:4:4 12-bit [pass osd] no 3d button needed; TaB L 12-bit [pass osd] no 3d button needed
#   FP 4:2:2 [pass]; FP 4:4:4 12-bit [pass osd]; 720p 4:4:4 [pass osd 12 bit]; 576p 4:4:4 [pass osd 12 bit]
#   480p 4:2:2 [pass]; 576p auto [pass osd 12 bit]; 640x480 F [pass osd 12 bit]
# Post-run review (Opus): the kernel journal of the test boot holds 8020 WARNINGs in gv100_head_state,
#   one per vblank during every 4:2:2 step and no other (60/s; 24/s in FP at 24 Hz). The branch's head
#   state readback warns on unknown pixel-depth codes and did not know the 4:2:2 ones (RAX=3 =
#   BPP_24_422). Readback only (its consumers are DP/LVDS paths); the picture was unaffected. Fixed in
#   ycbcr-poc patch 4 (tip 396725d9d), re-verified in run34. The "kernel:" lines below are attached to the
#   480p step by the old dmesg line-count filter, which the flood broke; the runner now counts warnings
#   per step from the journal.
#   The pre-flight "without CD=5" lines are the header of the A/B mode, absent in --ycbcr (no module swap).
